## ◈ 06 — INSTALLATION & EXECUTION

### Prerequisites

- Python 3.11+
- Node.js and npm (if required by the frontend)
- PostgreSQL (if required by the configured application)
- Git
- Visual Studio Code

### Step 01 — Clone Repository

```powershell
git clone https://github.com/Alwin0606/Opspilot-AI.git
```

### Step 02 — Navigate to Project

```powershell
cd Opspilot-AI
```

### Step 03 — Create Virtual Environment

```powershell
py -3.13 -m venv .venv
```

### Step 04 — Activate Environment

```powershell
Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope Process -ExecutionPolicy Bypass

.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
```

### Step 05 — Install Dependencies

If a `requirements.txt` file is available:

```powershell
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### Step 06 — Run Application

Use the startup command configured in the actual backend application.

For a FastAPI application with `main.py` exposing an `app` instance:

```powershell
python -m uvicorn main:app --reload
```

